# SignerOS users
#
# The GUI runs as an unprivileged user with no password, no valid shell and no
# supplementary groups. It reaches /dev/fb0, /dev/dri/*, /dev/input/* and
# /dev/tty0 because mdev.conf hands those nodes to group `signer`, not because
# the account is in `video`/`input` - that keeps the account's authority
# limited to exactly the nodes we name.
#
# It cannot mount, unmount or power off the machine. Requesting shutdown is
# done by exiting with status 42, which the root-owned session supervisor
# turns into a secure poweroff.
#
# <username> <uid> <group> <gid> <password> <home> <shell> <groups> <comment>
signer 1000 signer 1000 ! /home/signer /bin/false - SignerOS kiosk user
